{
  "dom_id": "step-q91941",
  "name": "Question 10",
  "problem": "There is a proportional relationship between the time $t$ (in seconds) that Jack runs and the distance $d$ (in meters) he covers.\n\n| Time ($t$) | Meters ($d$) |\n| --- | --- |\n| $1$ | $7$ |\n| $3$ | $21$ |\n| $5$ | $35$ |\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. Jack runs $35$ meters in $5$ seconds.\n\nII. The unit rate is $6$ meters per second.\n\nIII. If Jack runs for $7$ seconds, he covers $49$ meters.",
  "worked_solution": "We're told that $t$ and $d$ have a proportional relationship.\n\nTo find the constant of proportionality, we first need to choose a point $(t,d)$ from the table. Let's choose the point $(1,7),$ which corresponds to the first row of the table. \n\nWe can find the constant of proportionality as follows:\n\n$$\nk=\\frac{d}{t}=\\frac{7}{1}=7\n$$\n\nThe units of $k$ are \"meters per second\" since we divided the distance $d$ by the time $t.$ Therefore, the relationship between $d$ and $t$ is \n\n$$\nd=7t.\n$$\n\n  \n\nNow, with that in mind, let's look at each statement. \n\n- Statement I is true. The third row of the table corresponds to the point $(5,35),$ which means that if Jack runs for $5$ seconds, he covers $35$ meters.\n\n- Statement II is false. We know that $k=7,$ which means that the unit rate is $7$ meters per second.\n\n- Statement III is true. If we substitute $t=7$ into the relationship $d=7t,$ we get\n\n$$\nd=7\\cdot 7=49\n$$\n\nwhich means that If Jack runs for $7$ seconds, he covers $49$ meters.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only\".",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
